      },
      "lineNbr": 1349,
      "author": {
        "id": 1535516
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-05-09T00:49:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "that is a good idea, but it would be tricky to implement because if there wasn\u0027t a branch with the variable set, it would cause us to output these flags if the variable was or wasn\u0027t set when it should really be only when it\u0027s not set. For example:\n\n```\nsoong_config_variables: {\n  my_bool_var: {\n    conditions_default: {\n      target: {\n        android: {\n          cflags: [\"-DFOO\"],\n        },\n      },\n    },\n  },\n},\n```\nwould emit:\n```\nselect({\n  \"//build/bazel/os:android\": [\"-DFOO\"],\n  \"//conditions:default\": [],\n})\n```\nWhen the current implementation would emit:\n```\nselect({\n \n \"//build/bazel/product_variables:my_namespace__my_bool_variable__conditions_default__android\": [\"-DBAZ\"],\n  \"//conditions:default\": [],\n})\n```\nA more sophisticated implementation could emit this, but I\u0027d rather not tackle that complexity at the moment:\n```\nselect({\n  \"//build/bazel/product_variables:my_namespace__my_bool_variable__android\": [],\n  \"//build/bazel/os:android\": [\"-DFOO\"],\n  \"//conditions:default\": [],\n})\n```\n\nI filed b/281568854 to handle this in a followup.",
      "parentUuid": "a8e009ea_b0d30fe4",
